From 4729a54d51d497a7889b28dd2b428f85ae5fe9a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alisachen-google <alisa888cl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:31:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [TPU/PD] Release an aborted chunked prefill's kv row exactly
 once when the raiden sender must drain

A client disconnect during chunked prefill on a raiden prefill engine with the
radix cache off killed the engine:

    _drain_deferred_chunked_sender_aborts -> release_kv_cache
    AssertionError: Only a mamba-capable tree cache allows freeing before alloc

process_pending_chunked_abort parks the aborted request on
_deferred_chunked_sender_aborts because the transfer group still has native
I/O in flight, so its pages must stay allocated until raiden drains. The
in-flight chunk's result then reaches _retire_aborted_prefill_result, which
released the kv row anyway; on the next step the drain released it again and
ChunkCache's release precondition fired, taking every rank down.

Make the deferred list the single owner of the release:
_retire_aborted_prefill_result skips release_kv_cache while the request is
parked, and the drain guards the release the way the other abort sites already
do. Pages are no longer freed while raiden may still read them, and a parked
request whose row is already gone cannot assert.

Tests (existing files): the chunked-abort race test gains the drain orderings
(release exactly once, in the drain, for the overlap and non-overlap orderings;
immediate release when no drain is needed; two parked requests release
independently); the prefill abort-result cleanup test gains the parked case.
